  m_text: 'In automated production lines, the positioner is often controlled by a
    PLC (Programmable Logic Controller).


    The PLC sends signals to rotate the
    positioner to predefined angles based on the welding sequence.


    The robot
    and positioner operate in a fully synchronized loop, reducing cycle time and
    improving accuracy.'
