      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Dynamic Path Planning with MoveIt-Unlike static RAPID paths, ROS allows
    on-the-fly trajectory adjustments based on part position, heat buildup, or sensor
    feedback.\nThe robot can adjust its movements using inverse kinematics (IK) solvers
    to ensure optimal welding angles.\n\nSimulation & Collision Detection in Gazebo-The
    IRB 2600\u2019s movement and weld paths are validated in a ROS-Gazebo simulation
    before being applied in Unity.\nThis prevents errors, ensuring safe and optimized
    robot motions.\n\nReal-Time Sensor Feedback for Adaptive Welding-Laser scanners
    or depth cameras (e.g., Intel RealSense or LiDAR) detect part variations.\nForce-torque
    sensors adjust torch pressure to prevent welding defects.\n\nAI-powered defect
    detection can be integrated to optimize weld quality dynamically."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5b036e831c0c90547b32a8a896d80f79, type: 2}
